<%#
  Why a class is being called off.

  A partial because three pages offer it — the schedule's two halves
  and the register — and a list of reasons that says something
  different on one of them is worse than no list.

  The first option is blank on purpose. A select that starts on
  "Teacher unavailable" records "Teacher unavailable" for every teacher
  who did not look at it, which is a field that lies rather than a
  field that is empty. Nothing is assumed; the library refuses a
  cancellation that has neither a reason nor a note.

  Expects: cancelReasons.
%>
<label class="field">
  <span>Why — students see this</span>
  <select name="reason">
    <option value="">Choose a reason…</option>
    <% cancelReasons.forEach(function (r) { %>
      <option value="<%= r.key %>"><%= r.label %></option>
    <% }); %>
  </select>
</label>
